  "summary": "Toledo City Council is debating a resolution introduced by five members urging Mayor Wade Kapszukiewicz to terminate and not renew contracts with Flock Group, remove equipment, and delete collected data, citing surveillance and privacy concerns. Other council members call it premature, favoring awaiting results of an independent audit approved Sept. 22 and proposing separate guardrail legislation restricting searches and requiring warrants. A vote is expected Oct. 20.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A resolution, introduced by five council members, would urge Toledo Mayor Wade Kapszukiewicz to terminate and not renew any agreements with Flock Group, Inc. and its affiliates.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Toledo City Council unanimously approved an independent audit of the city's use and oversight of the Flock system on Sept. 22.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "it would restrict searchable terms to prohibit searches related to gender-affirming care and reproductive rights",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "Turning off the system before the findings are in would be like an umpire calling a pitch a strike before the ball is thrown.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    }
  ],
